/_[Aa]rchive/
/_[Dd]ata/

# Vendor modules. Each is a SEPARATE repository the user clones into this root - see
# COMPATIBILITY.md. Ignoring the path is what keeps the two git repos from colliding:
# no accidental gitlink, no `git add -A` swallowing a whole TwinCAT solution, and a
# `git status` here that stays quiet about a checkout it does not own.
#
# Add a line when you add a module to _workflow/config/modules.json.
/Beckhoff/
/Siemens/

# The engineering TOOLS that read the Unity export, and their own separate repository:
# the Python that generates _docs/context/ and checks the wiring.
#
# The line is what a tool READS, not that it is Python. The WIKI tooling is public, in
# _workflow/tools/ - it reads only tracked files, and .github/workflows/wiki.yml has to
# run it from a checkout of this repository alone. Everything else that describes how
# the project is built - the skills, the workflow guideline, CONTEXT-SPEC.md,
# WIKI-SPEC.md, CLAUDE.md and the module declaration - is in _workflow/ and tracked,
# because a reader who wants to know how this project is built should be able to.
/_private/

# There is deliberately no .claude/ in this project - _workflow/ is the one folder
# that holds the agent material, and the skills there are read by path rather than
# auto-discovered. This rule is a guard: if a tool ever creates .claude/ here, it is
# scratch and must not be committed.
/.claude/
/_workflow/settings.local.json

# Generated documentation. build_wiki.py flattens _docs/ and every knowledge base into
# _wiki/, which made it a second committed copy of ~6700 lines that already exist in
# this repo. It is rebuilt on demand and published by publish_wiki.py.
/_wiki/

**/scheduled_tasks.lock
__pycache__/
